<p>The number of students earning an undergraduate degree in philosophy in the United States declined for the third year in a row.<span id="more-57370"></span></p>
<p>According to new data from <a href="https://www.amacad.org/humanities-indicators" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Humanities Indicators</a>, a project of the <a href="https://www.amacad.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">American Academy of Arts &amp; Sciences</a>, US universities and colleges issued 5,763 bachelor&#8217;s degrees in philosophy in 2024, compared with 5,998 in 2023, 6380 in 2022, and 6,757 in 2021.</p>
<div id="attachment_57371" style="width: 781px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-57371" class=" wp-image-57371" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bachelors-degrees-in-philosophy-rates.png" alt="" width="771" height="600" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bachelors-degrees-in-philosophy-rates.png 1869w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bachelors-degrees-in-philosophy-rates-300x234.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bachelors-degrees-in-philosophy-rates-1024x798.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bachelors-degrees-in-philosophy-rates-768x598.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bachelors-degrees-in-philosophy-rates-1536x1197.png 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/bachelors-degrees-in-philosophy-rates-400x312.png 400w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 771px) 100vw, 771px" /><p id="caption-attachment-57371" class="wp-caption-text">[graph from Humanities Indicators. Original interactive version <a href="https://www.amacad.org/humanities-indicators/higher-education/bachelors-degrees-humanities" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.]</p></div>Though the changes have been small from year to year, there has been a roughly 14.7% decrease in undergraduate philosophy degrees conferred between 2021 and 2024.</p>
<p>During the same period of time, the share of all bachelor&#8217;s degrees that went to students majoring in any humanities fields dropped from 9.3% to 8.4%, a drop of around 9%.</p>
